export const ASK_PACK: readonly AskChunk[] = [{"id":1,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): Purser","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#purser","text":"AI agents pay your suppliers within the limits the CFO sets; above a limit nothing runs until the CFO's passkey (Face ID) signs the exact terms: one changed cent and the approval no longer matches the terms.\nPurser is the control layer between a company's AI agents and its money on Airwallex and Alta (formerly Metal); everything here ran on test money, in sandboxes and on testnet.\n\nAI agents spend. You sign off. Built for the Airwallex Agentic Banking Hackathon: Starter Kit 11 (x402 Business Agents), entered for the Metal Award and the Visa Award, and for the Founder's Choice Award and the Judges' Choice Award."},
{"id":2,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): In one minute","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#in-one-minute","text":"- What it is: Claude agents read, check and propose supplier payments; Purser's code enforces the CFO's limits; above a limit the CFO signs a SHA-256 of the exact terms (payee, amount, account, FX quote, fee ceiling) with a passkey before any money call. The payment then goes out through Airwallex, carrying that hash in its own record, and is booked (double-entry, VAT, month close).\n- Who it is for: the finance team of a small company that banks with Airwallex and pays suppliers abroad. That buyer is a hypothesis: there are no customers yet, and nothing here has moved real money.\n- What is live: Claude's decisions, Airwallex sandbox calls, Alta testnet transactions, Visa Intelligent Commerce via Airwallex Airi (sandbox, test card) and the T:0 sandbox ledger. Every run is dated, with its record: https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/runs\n- Simulated: the customer, the supplier, the merchants' charges, the settlement (Purser moves the SWIFT transfer to SENT, then PAID, through the sandbox's simulation API) and the second approver (a labelled test passkey).\n- Not done yet: real money, real customers, an independent security audit. …"},
{"id":3,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): Check these first (each with its record)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#check-these-first-each-with-its-record","text":"- The CFO's signed hash inside Airwallex's own transfer record (metadata.approval_sha256, read back from the sandbox): https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/airwallex#awx-hash\n- 30 signed payments in a row on 20 Nov, each read back from Airwallex as signed, and 5 one-cent changes refused before any create (sandbox; PAID by the sandbox's simulation): https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/runs/2026-11-20-airwallex-soak.md\n- The same create sent again under one request_id: Airwallex refused all 9 repeats and kept one object per request_id; two of its answers were codes Purser did not yet read as duplicates, fixed the same day (sandbox, 20 Nov): https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/runs/2026-11-20-airwallex-replay.md …"},
{"id":4,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): For judges: watch, try, verify","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#for-judges-watch-try-verify","text":"1. Watch the demo (3:15): https://youtu.be/gEUm8RlhZac\n2. Try it (2 minutes, test money): https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/try: the agent pays EUR 120.00 alone; you sign EUR 1,850.00 with a passkey; the same payment with one cent changed is refused; download its proof file and check it on https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/verify\n3. Verify in 3 commands, offline, no keys (Node.js 22.13+, after git clone https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents): npm ci, npm run judge -- --check (every page built from the main run's record), npm run verify-approval (the owner's real passkey approval of 7 November, checked with Node's crypto)\n4. All the evidence on one page: https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/proof#evidence (the evidence wall below, as tiles), every live run on https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/runs"},
{"id":5,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): The evidence wall, from the records","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#the-evidence-wall-from-the-records","text":"Written by npm run evidence:wall from the committed records; the same figures, each linked to its record, are on https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/proof#evidence. Test money only; what was simulated is said on each line.\n\nLive on the rails:\n- All 132 Airwallex transfers PAID from the public /try (sandbox; 67 walks as a visitor, 19 Nov to 21 Nov; PAID by the sandbox's simulation): https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/runs/2026-11-21-phone-try/summary.json\n- All 3 paid invoices made bills in Airwallex Spend (sandbox; the signed hash as external_id, read back exactly; transfers PAID by the sandbox's simulation, 19 Nov): https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/runs/2026-11-19-airwallex-bills.md\n- All 60 soak payments PAID, signed hash read back (sandbox; each read back from Airwallex as signed: hash, amount, payee, reference; PAID by the sandbox's simulation; 2 soaks, 19 and 20 Nov): https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/runs/2026-11-20-airwallex-soak.md …"},
{"id":6,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): Connect an AI (MCP): read and propose only","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#connect-an-ai-mcp-read-and-propose-only","text":"- Connect any AI: Purser Cloud is a remote MCP server at https://purser-try.max-31b.workers.dev/mcp; the demo company's public, read-only token is purser-demo-read-only. Your AI reads and can propose a payment; it can never approve or pay: docs/connect-claude.md; every tool, its annotations, the error codes and the safety model: docs/mcp.md\n- No MCP tool approves, pays, changes a limit or writes to the books: every payment needs the CFO's passkey in Purser Cloud. The demo company is made-up data from a simulated month, no real money.\n- Connect Purser to anything: every way in or out, each with its honest label (live, sandbox, testnet, format export, built and not tested live, planned), a quickstart and its guide: the payment rails, AI over MCP, the REST API and its OpenAPI, signed webhooks, no-code tools, accounting, Peppol, ISO 20022, Slack and Teams, the full export: https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md (the same list as JSON: GET /v1/connections on Purser Cloud)"},
{"id":7,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): Security posture: self-assessments, not audits","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#security-posture-self-assessments-not-audits","text":"- No independent audit or penetration test has been done. What exists is written by the project itself: an OWASP ASVS 4.0.3 Level 2 self-assessment (190 pass, 22 fail of the 212 requirements that apply, 19 Nov; written with Claude, not verified by anyone independent): https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security/asvs-l2.md\n- The threat model, each control with its evidence, and the risks still open (accepted risks included): https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md\n- OpenSSF Best Practices: Silver, from the project's own answers to the programme's criteria (project 16923, as of 19 Nov; the live status is on the project page): https://www.bestpractices.dev/projects/16923\n- Security and trust: https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/security (each control with its proof, and what is not in place yet; sandbox and testnet only)"},
{"id":8,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): Product pages","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#product-pages","text":"- /try (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/try): a test company of your own; Claude reads an invoice, the Checker agent's tool calls are shown with its model, timing and cost, you sign the exact terms with a passkey, then one cent more is refused\n- /airwallex (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/airwallex): cards per agent with the CFO policy as Airwallex's controls, read back; Airwallex's own declines; SWIFT payouts carrying the signed hash; FX for the shortfall only. Its API coverage, each endpoint LIVE (a committed record holds a call), TESTED ONLY or CODE ONLY: https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/evidence/airwallex-api-coverage.md\n- /alta (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/alta): Alta (formerly Metal) testnet: a mandate on chain per agent; the main run's 86 payments, each its own transaction; purchase #24 refused on chain after we switched off our own check once to test the chain (/metal answers 301 to it)\n- /visa (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/visa): Visa Intelligent Commerce through Airwallex's Airi, sandbox and a test card; Visa is named for the rail only, no endorsement implied …"},
{"id":9,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): Key run records","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#key-run-records","text":"- docs/runs/README.md (https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/runs/README.md): every live run, newest first, with its ids and what was simulated\n- The main run, 3 November (https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/runs/2026-11-03-main-run.md): three Claude agents run a test company for a day on Alta testnet and the Airwallex sandbox; the run the site replays (docs/demo/main-run.json)\n- The Airwallex-only run (https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/runs/2026-11-07-awx-1.md): Airwallex's own card controls declined an agent's EUR 45.00 purchase (charge simulated via the sandbox) over its EUR 30.00 limit (LIMIT_EXCEEDED, card transaction 01a1b5e8-6dc2-7000-95bf-c8fc5e6e2f38; 7 November; all seven checks passed) …"},
{"id":10,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): Pilots and partnerships","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#pilots-and-partnerships","text":"Pilots, partnerships and questions: max.geurtsen@outlook.com. Purser has no customers yet and runs on test money only."},
{"id":11,"doc":"llms.txt","title":"Purser in one page (llms.txt): For agents","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/llms.txt#for-agents","text":"- Proof as JSON: https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/proof.json. A signed receipt you can check offline: https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/receipt-sample.json\n- To check a receipt: write the terms as canonical JSON (keys sorted, money as decimal strings); its SHA-256 equals terms_sha256; that hash is the WebAuthn challenge in clientDataJSON; the ES256 signature verifies with public_key. In a clone: npm run verify-receipt -- docs/runs/2026-11-07-awx-1/receipt-P-0002.json\n- The sample is the owner's own passkey approval of 7 November (live, Airwallex sandbox, test money; Face ID, as stated by the owner): the receipt does not prove who holds the key, or that it was Face ID (no attestation is checked).\n- An outside agent can ask for a company card and pay within limits over MCP (npm run mcp, docs/agent-api.md). Only a person's passkey can approve.\n- skills/purser-spend/SKILL.md: how an outside agent should use the agent API"},
{"id":12,"doc":"README.md","title":"README: Purser · AI agents spend. You sign off.","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/README.md#purser--ai-agents-spend-you-sign-off","text":"AI agents pay your suppliers. Above their limit, you sign the exact terms with your passkey: one changed cent and the approval no longer matches the terms.\n\n1 · Watch the demo (3:15) (https://youtu.be/gEUm8RlhZac) · 2 · Try it live on /try (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/try) (2 min, test money) · 3 · See the proof on /proof (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/proof)\nSponsor track | What ran live (test money) | Record\nAirwallex (sandbox) | Main run, 3 Nov: an agent's EUR 240.00 SWIFT payment; Airwallex's own transfer record carries the hash of the exact terms the CFO signed (metadata.approval_sha256, read back 6 Nov) | transfer record\nVisa via Airwallex's Airi (sandbox, test card) | 14 Nov: EUR 45.00 above the CFO's limit, paid with a Visa credential bound to that one purchase, only after the CFO's passkey; reused, or for another amount, refused by Purser before any call | run log\nAlta (formerly Metal) (testnet) | Main run, 3 Nov: x402 agents buy and sell data under on-chain mandates, 86 Alta payments; purchase #24, over its mandate, refused on chain by Alta itself | run log\nT:0 (shared sandbox ledger) | 14 Nov: all 95 of the main run's journal entries read back from T:0, every …"},
{"id":13,"doc":"README.md","title":"README: The proof","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/README.md#the-proof","text":"Evidence wall, from the records: All 60 soak payments read back · All 132 /try payouts PAID · All 894 forged copies refused · 71 Airwallex endpoints live · every figure, with its record (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/proof#evidence) · the index of /proof's figures\nFor judges: the four things every entry shows, and where every id is | Check it\nUser: a CFO whose AI agents pay suppliers; above an agent's limit, the CFO signs | /try (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/try) · for the CFO\nAirwallex action: a SWIFT transfer that carries the hash of the signed terms in metadata.approval_sha256 (main run of 3 Nov, read back from Airwallex on 6 Nov) | record\nFinancial context: the agent spends only what is available (balance − holds − payouts in flight), above a cash floor; FX buys only the shortfall | available.ts · treasury.ts\nControls: per-agent limits; a passkey over the exact terms; duplicates held; a payout that fails after PAID goes back to a person | approvals.ts · euroBill.ts · follow.ts\nProof: one id per rail, and every run with its record, live or simulated | one id per rail · every run · /proof (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/proof) …"},
{"id":14,"doc":"README.md","title":"README: How it works","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/README.md#how-it-works","text":"An approval is usually a button. In Purser it's a signature over the exact terms: change one cent and it's worthless.\n1 · The agent asks | 2 · Code checks the limit | 3 · You sign the exact terms\nA Claude agent proposes a payment: an invoice, a card charge, an x402 purchase. | Within the CFO's limits it pays alone; Airwallex and Alta hold the limit again. | Above them, the CFO's passkey (Face ID on iPhone) signs the SHA-256 of the exact terms.\nAbove your limit: not signed, never paid.\n\n- A passkey signs the exact terms. The approval is a signature over the SHA-256 of the terms; change one cent and it no longer verifies. The owner's real approval of 7 November is checked offline by npm run verify-approval (record).\n- Limits are enforced in 3 layers: Purser's code, Airwallex's card controls and Alta's on-chain mandate. Airwallex itself declined an agent's card over the CFO's limit (record); Alta refused a purchase over the mandate on chain (record). The mandates: /api/metal/mandates (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/api/metal/mandates), a live read from Alta testnet, or the recorded 12 Nov snapshot when the chain does not answer (the answer says which). …"},
{"id":15,"doc":"README.md","title":"README: Built with","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/README.md#built-with","text":"Partner | What Purser uses | Live or simulated | Proof\nAirwallex (sandbox) | agent cards and limits, FX, SWIFT payouts, its approval as a second lock, the payee name check | Sandbox, live calls; SWIFT settlement simulated through the sandbox's simulation API | the card decline, two locks, name check\nAlta (testnet) | a mandate per agent, x402 payments, limits changed only by two passkeys, the audit anchor | Testnet, live transactions, test money | main run, two passkeys, series, anchor\nVisa Intelligent Commerce via Airwallex's Airi (sandbox, test card) | a Visa credential bound to one purchase; above the limit only after the CFO's passkey | Airwallex sandbox, live calls, test card; a headless browser typed the card into Airwallex's hosted page | vic-3, vic-4, vic-5\nClaude by Anthropic | the agents' decisions (Haiku, Sonnet, Opus) and the invoice reader; code checks each | Live calls | main run, /claude (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/claude)\nT:0 (shared sandbox entity) | an outside ledger: the main run's 95 journal entries, checked against our books: every account to the cent, plus the entry count | Shared sandbox ledger, live calls, test balances | posted, read back\nNo …"},
{"id":16,"doc":"README.md","title":"README: Verify it yourself in 3 commands","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/README.md#verify-it-yourself-in-3-commands","text":"The quick start: under 2 minutes, no keys. Needs Node.js 22.13+ (or 23.4+) and git. npm ci downloads packages from npm; after that, no network and no keys.\n\nVerify it yourself, offline: npm run verify-approval checks the real approval; change one cent in a copy and npm run verify-receipt -- tampered.json says NOT VALID. Below, the real output of both.\n\nWhat you should see (abridged). \n\nnpm run verify-receipt -- receipt.json\nchecks any receipt of the same format. npm run airwallex-trail lists the Airwallex sandbox API calls in the run records it reads and re-checks, offline, that each transfer carries the hash the passkey signed (exit 1 on any mismatch; the same list is on /airwallex/calls (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/airwallex/calls)). Pay on /try (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/try), download the proof (JSON), and check it on /verify (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/verify) in your browser, or with npm run verify-bundle -- purser-proof.json: the same checks, the same code, no server (samples). …"},
{"id":17,"doc":"README.md","title":"README: Try it in 2 minutes","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/README.md#try-it-in-2-minutes","text":"1. Pay an invoice yourself: kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/try (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/try). A test company of your own; Claude reads a sample invoice, you approve the exact terms with your own passkey, it is paid on a simulated bank and booked. Change what you signed: refused.\n2. Look around a company: Purser Cloud as a guest (https://purser-try.max-31b.workers.dev/), then Try as guest: the demo company's dashboard and books, read-only, made-up data, test money.\n3. Ask your own AI: add the remote MCP server https://purser-try.max-31b.workers.dev/mcp and choose the demo company (public token purser-demo-read-only): ask \"what's waiting for the CFO?\". It reads; it cannot approve or pay (Connect any AI). Everything else Purser connects to, each labelled: Connect Purser to anything.\n\nFrom code, the same question: the TypeScript and Python clients (sdk/typescript, sdk/python), no dependencies, run from a clone: not published to npm or PyPI. They take an API key with the read scope (the demo token works at /mcp only). Neither can approve."},
{"id":18,"doc":"README.md","title":"README: The business hypothesis","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/README.md#the-business-hypothesis","text":"Not validated with customers yet: 2 finance conversations (a CFO and a bank finance professional, quoted, anonymous); more in progress; no pilots, no revenue. Every line below is a hypothesis except the cited source.\n\n- The problem: when an AI agent pays today, its limit lives in a prompt it can be talked out of, or in a month-end review that finds the money after it has left. (problem.md)\n- Who buys: the finance team of a small company or scale-up that already banks with Airwallex and lets AI agents pay; the CFO uses it and decides. (model.md)\n- Pilot pricing: Starter €49 a month (100 invoices, then €0.25 each); Business from €249 a month; a small fee per payout. A hypothesis. (model.md)\n- Why now: Airwallex wrote on 5 October 2026 that agents moving money need limits enforced \"through underlying infrastructure rather than prompts\" (\"Agentic banking starts with governance\", source S1). (problem.md)\n- Why Purser: it builds on Airwallex's own card controls and Alta's mandates, and adds what sits on top: one CFO policy for card and chain, approvals signed over the exact terms, a hash-chained audit log. …"},
{"id":19,"doc":"README.md","title":"README: More","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/README.md#more","text":"The demo (3:15) (https://youtu.be/gEUm8RlhZac), the video in the submission (its thumbnail is at the top) · test money only\n\nEarlier videos: the film, under the hood (3:29) (https://youtu.be/PNLuqhRzVfE) · the trailer (1:30) (https://youtu.be/n3HLVGROJc4) · test money only\nTopic | In one line | Where\nGallery | The pages and the console, as screenshots | docs/gallery.md\nVisa Award | Purser's Visa Award entry: Visa Intelligent Commerce through Airwallex's Airi, sandbox | docs/visa-award.md\nEnterprise | What a finance team gets beyond the demo, test money today | docs/enterprise.md\nSee it | The hands-on demo as a clip, and each page's first screen | docs/see-it.md\nHow it works in 5 files | The five files that make a payment safe, and the policy's worst case | docs/how-it-works.md\nProof in numbers | The charts, drawn from the run records | docs/charts.md\nConnect any AI | Connect Claude or any MCP client to the demo company's books: it reads and proposes, never approves or pays | docs/mcp.md · docs/connect-any-ai.md\nConnect to anything | Every way in or out, each with its honest label and a quickstart: payment rails, AI over MCP, the API and webhooks, no-code tools, accounting, Peppol, …"},
{"id":20,"doc":"docs/how-it-works.md","title":"How it works: How it works in 5 files","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#how-it-works-in-5-files","text":"The code in 5 files, one payment end to end, and the worst case the policy allows.\n\nMoved from the README on 15 November, to keep it short.\n\nNorthwind Outdoor, the example company, is an outdoor wholesaler that sells live stock data to retailers per query: the\nkit's data business. Purser gives each AI agent of a small company its own Airwallex card and its own Alta (formerly Metal) on-chain mandate. Alta holds\neach agent's on-chain budget, Airwallex holds each card's limit, Purser's code holds the rest; the CFO approves anything\nbeyond them, with a passkey (Face ID on iPhone) on the exact terms.\n\nClaude agents propose and pay; Purser's code, Airwallex and Alta each hold a limit; above them, the CFO signs the exact terms with a passkey (Face ID on iPhone)."},
{"id":21,"doc":"docs/how-it-works.md","title":"How it works: One payment beyond the limit, end to end","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#one-payment-beyond-the-limit-end-to-end","text":"Within the limits an agent pays on its own; beyond them, nothing runs without the CFO's passkey."},
{"id":22,"doc":"docs/how-it-works.md","title":"How it works: The worst case the policy allows","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#the-worst-case-the-policy-allows","text":"Worst case, set by policy: EUR 28,200 on cards and task cards + USD 20 on chain a month.\n\nTask cards under a CFO-signed limit: EUR 900 a day. Everything above waits for the CFO.\n\nHow this is computed. \n\n- Sourcing agent: EUR 100 on its card + USD 10 on chain (test USD) a month.\n- Support agent: EUR 150 on its card + USD 4 on chain (test USD) a month.\n- Treasury agent: EUR 50 on its card + EUR 27,900 in task cards + USD 6 on chain (test USD) a month.\n- A day: EUR 1,200 + USD 20: a card or a mandate can go in one day, task cards 3 a day.\n- Counted: each card's monthly limit (card.*.monthly, EUR) and each Alta mandate's budget (test USD, *USDZ; it lasts 40 days and can all go at once). Task cards, which the Treasury agent may issue on its own within the limit the CFO signed with Face ID: up to EUR 300 each (approval.task_card_eur), 3 a day (EUR 900), 31 days a month (EUR 27,900), counted above.\n- ≈ EUR 28,217.70 in all at the main run's rate of 3 Nov 2026 (1.129917 USD per EUR, docs/demo/main-run.json); test USD is never added to EUR otherwise.\n- With a shared card or an API key, the limit is the card's or the account's. …"},
{"id":23,"doc":"docs/how-it-works.md","title":"How it works: The code in 5 files","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#the-code-in-5-files","text":"Each name below links to the line that defines it; a test fails if that line moves.\n\n1. The policy. reserveSpend runs before an agent's payment is signed or charged: its identity, the CFO's stops and caps, the mandate's cap and budget, the shared 20.00 total and velocity. A refusal means nothing is signed.\n2. The terms hash and the passkey. termsHash is the SHA-256 of a proposal's exact terms as canonical JSON; verifyApprovalSignature accepts a passkey's signature only if it signed that hash, with user verification (Face ID) on.\n3. The executors' hash check. Every executor in src/executors/ starts with beginExecution, which re-hashes the stored terms and runs nothing unless they match the approved hash, before the expiry, and (since 20 November) re-verifies the stored passkey signatures behind the approval over those exact terms.\n4. The Alta mandate layer. payUnderMandate signs an x402 payment with the agent's own mandate key only after the caller's guard passes it (Sourcing's is reserveSpend); on chain, Alta refuses what is over the mandate.\n5. The audit chain. …"},
{"id":24,"doc":"docs/cfo-policy.md","title":"The CFO's policy: The CFO policy","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/cfo-policy.md#the-cfo-policy","text":"The limits the agents work within, set by the CFO and changed only with the CFO's Face ID.\n\nMoved from the project README. Back to the README."},
{"id":25,"doc":"docs/cfo-policy.md","title":"The CFO's policy: CFO policy","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/cfo-policy.md#cfo-policy","text":"The CFO sets limits the agents work within: each agent's company card limits (per purchase and per month, synced to\nthe card at Airwallex), and inside their on-chain mandates a limit per payment for each agent,\nthe refund amounts above which a person must approve, the EUR and USD reserve floors, which Airwallex payees\nare allowed, and up to which amount a task card is issued without Face ID (\"Task cards up to this\nare issued without Face ID\", approval.task_card_eur, 300.00 EUR to start; see ask-purser.md). Each is checked before anything is signed: the sourcing agent aborts the x402 payment when the\nsupplier's offer is over its limit (policy_cap_exceeded, nothing signed, the customer not charged), refunds and\nsweeps refuse before the pull, and an invoice to a blocked payee escalates. The mandates stay the hard outer wall;\nthe policy can only be stricter.\n\nA change is a policy_change proposal that names the value it replaces. …"},
{"id":26,"doc":"docs/cfo-policy.md","title":"The CFO's policy: What would have happened (the policy simulator)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/cfo-policy.md#what-would-have-happened-the-policy-simulator","text":"Before signing, the CFO sees what the change would have done to the recent payments. npm run policy -- simulate\n= ... [--since YYYY-MM-DD] replays the period's supplier payments (the last 30 days by default) under the\npolicy now and with the change, with Purser's own decision code, and lists each payment that would change: now paid\nalone, now needing the CFO, or now refused, with why. Example: npm run policy -- simulate ap.alone_eur=1000.00\n\"counterparty:Bergtex Textil GmbH=blocked\" (none removes an optional limit). A waiting policy change shows the same\none line on the runner's dashboard and on the phone's approval page (\"If this had been in force since …: N payments\nwould have …\"); it is not part of the terms the passkey signs. The replay writes nothing and calls nothing; what it\ncannot know (an agent's judgement) is in governance.md."},
{"id":27,"doc":"docs/cfo-policy.md","title":"The CFO's policy: The Agents page","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/cfo-policy.md#the-agents-page","text":"The dashboard's Agents tab (?agents, also in the recorded run as ?recorded&agents) shows each agent on one\npanel, all read from the same CFO policy the agents are held to (src/agents/profiles.ts; the page keeps no copy):\n\n- its job, and whether it is working, stopped (its own stop, for example a velocity limit) or frozen (the emergency stop);\n- the Claude model for each of its jobs (Haiku sorts documents, Sonnet reads them, Opus reviews its proposals), from\n the same list the tools call (CLAUDE_JOBS in src/claude/tools.ts; a test keeps the two equal);\n- its company card (per purchase, per month, merchant categories), its Metal mandate and the policy's limit inside it,\n and its speed limit (payments a minute, amounts an hour);\n- what it does on its own, and what waits for the CFO's Face ID, with the policy's current numbers;\n- its settings, as the policy editor shows them.\n\nChanging a setting follows the policy's rules, unchanged: tightening (a lower limit, stopping the agent) is done\non the phone, opened for that agent (/policy?agent=, or &stop=on to stop it), signed with Face ID and applied\nat once. …"},
{"id":28,"doc":"docs/cfo-policy.md","title":"The CFO's policy: The CFO policy in plain words","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/cfo-policy.md#the-cfo-policy-in-plain-words","text":"The CFO writes the policy as they would say it, for example \"the sourcing agent's card at most €25 per purchase;\nrefunds above 0.05 I want to see\". This works on the runner (npm run policy -- from-text \"…\") or in the box at the\ntop of the phone's policy page.\n\n1. Opus maps each sentence onto the existing settings. For each rule it gives the exact words the rule rests on. A\n sentence that fits no single setting comes back with a question instead.\n2. Code keeps a rule only if:\n - its setting exists;\n - its quote is copied from the CFO's text;\n - its amount is written in that quote (Opus may not split, add up or round);\n - its value passes the setting's limits.\n\n From the phone, a rule that would loosen the policy is refused, just as in the policy editor.\n3. The rules that are left become one policy-change proposal. The approval page shows which words gave which rule.\n Nothing changes until the CFO approves it with Face ID.\n\nTried live with Opus. It mapped two of four sentences and asked about the other two. One gave an amount in euros for\na setting in *USDZ. The other asked for a total across all three cards, which no single setting holds."},
{"id":29,"doc":"docs/cfo-policy.md","title":"The CFO's policy: Four eyes: two people above a threshold","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/cfo-policy.md#four-eyes-two-people-above-a-threshold","text":"The CFO policy setting \"Payments above this need two people\" (approval.four_eyes_eur) is off by default. Once\nit is set, these proposals need the Face ID of two different people, each with their own passkey:\n\n- an invoice payment above the threshold;\n- an outside agent's card with a monthly limit above it;\n- a supplier's new bank details, at any amount.\n\nThe rules:\n\n- The first approval is kept, and the proposal waits. The phone shows \"1 of 2\" and who has signed so far.\n- The same person approving twice does not count.\n- Whoever proposed it can never approve it.\n- One person's rejection stops it.\n- A typed hash prefix can never meet the rule.\n- npm run verify checks both signatures again, from two different people.\n\nTo add a second person, run npm run passkey -- add anna on the runner. Anna opens /enrol on her own phone and\ntypes the code. Then confirm the fingerprint her phone shows with npm run passkey -- confirm .\n\nEach person has one active passkey. Replacing yours leaves the others alone.\n\nTurning four eyes on, or lowering its threshold, tightens the policy. Turning it off, or raising the threshold, needs a\nproposal and Face ID."},
{"id":30,"doc":"docs/cfo-policy.md","title":"The CFO's policy: Emergency stop and changed bank details","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/cfo-policy.md#emergency-stop-and-changed-bank-details","text":"- Emergency stop.\n - The dashboard's Emergency stop opens the CFO policy on the phone with freeze set. One Face ID then does two\n things:\n - every agent payment is refused before anything is signed (supplier purchases, refunds, sweeps, invoice\n payments, prepaid clearing offers);\n - every company card is set INACTIVE at Airwallex, which declines with CARD_INACTIVE (checked live).\n - Pulling it tightens the policy, so the phone may do it. Lifting it loosens the policy, so it needs a proposal and\n Face ID.\n - While it is on, the dashboard shows a red band saying who pulled it, when and why.\n\n- A supplier's new bank details (npm run payee). Changed bank details are how invoice fraud works, so a new IBAN\n is paid only after three separate steps:\n 1. a request, which changes nothing;\n 2. a person records that the supplier confirmed the account on a contact already in our own records (an agent\n cannot do this);\n 3. a proposal with the full new IBAN and that verification, approved with Face ID.\n\n Only then is the account added at Airwallex and made the supplier's active payee. The old account is kept as\n REPLACED."},
{"id":31,"doc":"docs/phone-approval.md","title":"Approving with Face ID: Dashboard","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/phone-approval.md#dashboard","text":"npm run dashboard serves a live view of the ledger at http://127.0.0.1:4300 (set KIT11_DB to pick a world).\nIt polls every 2 seconds, shows Live or Stale, and fits one screen on a laptop and one column on a phone.\nPanel | What it shows\nWaiting for approval | Every proposal that waits for a person: plain-language summary, countdown to expiry, hash prefix, Opus's advisory verdict, and a link to the approval page. Below it, the latest closed proposals.\nAgent budgets | Each agent's Metal mandate: spent of budget, what is left, the cap per payment, the payee, how often it was replaced (spend carries over), and the 20.00 split across agents.\nTreasury | Free EUR above the reserve floor and committed bills, USD above its floor (Airwallex, from the last balance read), and the Metal earnings swept to Airwallex.\nRefusals and escalations | Every refused purchase, escalated invoice, late approval, expired or rejected proposal, with its reason in plain words.\nAgent activity | The audit log as sentences, newest first, with the agent, the Claude model where one was used, explorer links for chain transactions and Airwallex ids. …"},
{"id":32,"doc":"docs/phone-approval.md","title":"Approving with Face ID: Approving on a phone with a passkey","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/phone-approval.md#approving-on-a-phone-with-a-passkey","text":"The dashboard and the approvals also run on one fixed address, https://kit11..workers.dev, so the CFO\ncan approve from a phone with Face ID. The passkey signs the SHA-256 of the exact terms: the challenge is the hash's\n32 bytes, so a signature is worth something for those terms only, and any change after signing makes it worthless.\n\n- The relay cannot approve anything. It is a Cloudflare Worker with one SQLite Durable Object (worker/): it\n serves the pages, keeps the state the runner last pushed and queues what the phone submits. It holds no key. The\n runner (npm run relay) pulls each submission and verifies it with @simplewebauthn/server against the pinned\n public key: the challenge must be the proposal's terms hash, the origin and rpId the relay's host, user\n verification on, the counter not going back. Only then does it record the approval (method passkey, approver\n max (passkey )) and run the executor. The relay's own checks (same-origin posts, the exact hash, expiry,\n queue and per-address limits) only refuse early.\n- The phone checks the hash too. …"},
{"id":33,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#security-and-threat-model","text":"What Purser protects, who might attack it and how, what stops each attack, and what is out of scope.\n\nThe system lets AI agents buy, sell, refund and pay bills on their own, within limits, and asks a person for\neverything else. This page lists what we protect, who might attack it and how, what stops each attack, and what is\nout of scope. It covers our own system only. Every claim below points to code or to a test. Updated on 2 November for\nwhat was added since 30 October: the autonomous agents, D24 origins, MFA sessions, the TAP plan and test-money\nrecycling (rows 31 to 38), and the headers and rate limits as the code serves them. The controls in SOC 2 form, with\ntheir evidence and what is not in place: controls.md. Corrected on 12 November from the zero-trust\nmatrix (rows 8, 9, 15, 19 and 23, and the accepted risks). The rows have not been re-read in full since 12 November:\ntheir content is as of that date. The pinned versions and the bill of materials are in\nsecurity/README.md, updated on 19 November. Hardened on 19 November (row 17, least privilege, and the public demo's bot check):\nsecurity/2026-11-19-hardening.md. …"},
{"id":34,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: What we protect","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#what-we-protect","text":"Asset | Where it lives\nTreasury: *USDZ on Alta (formerly Metal) testnet, EUR and USD in the Airwallex sandbox | on chain; Airwallex\nAgent mandate keys and credentials, the owner key | the private keys repo (x402-business-agents-keys), never in this repo or a model\nAPI credentials: Airwallex key, Alta RPC URL, Anthropic key, Cloudflare token, relay token | environment secrets only\nThe CFO's passkey | his iPhone (iCloud Keychain); the ledger pins its public key\nThe ledger: proposals, approvals, the hash-chained audit log, the beneficiary allowlist, the CFO policy | SQLite on the runner"},
{"id":35,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Trust boundaries","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#trust-boundaries","text":"Everything left of the runner is untrusted input. That includes every document, every model answer, and the\nrelay with whatever it queues. Only the runner holds payment keys and writes the ledger. Purser Cloud keeps each\ncompany's connected-account OAuth tokens sealed (AES-256-GCM, bound to that company; cloud/src/sealed.ts). Claude asks for actions only\nthrough a fixed set of tools per agent; code checks every call, and the zero-trust report lists the tools each flow\noffered a hostile model.\n\nThe same boundaries as a diagram (added 19 November; GitHub draws it from Mermaid). Each box is one trust zone; an\narrow that crosses a box's edge is a boundary, and its label says what crosses and what checks it."},
{"id":36,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Zero trust, layer by layer","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#zero-trust-layer-by-layer","text":"The limits are enforced in layers that do not trust each other, and one matrix attacks them layer by layer on the real\ncode. Each attack starts with part of the system already in the attacker's hands, and its test shows which layer\noutside the attacker's reach still stops the money. The matrix ran against stand-ins of the rails in this\nrepository's test harness, not against the live rails; where a run record shows the live rail refusing in the same\nway, the report cites it. The layers, every attack with its evidence, the coverage, the depth of each way money\nleaves, the stand-ins and the open risks are in zero-trust.md, and as data in\nzero-trust/report.json. npm run zero-trust writes both from src/zerotrust/model.ts and a\nrun of test/zero-trust.test.ts; that test fails when they differ. The numbers are there, not here."},
{"id":37,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Attackers and attacks","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#attackers-and-attacks","text":"The STRIDE column names the kind of threat each row is, read from its attack (added 19 November): Spoofing (acting\nas someone else), Tampering (changing data, terms or state), Repudiation (denying or hiding who did what),\nInformation disclosure, Denial of service (including running up a bill), Elevation of privilege (doing more\nthan the limits allow).\n# | Attacker | Attack | STRIDE | What stops it | Proof\n1 | Fake supplier (BEC) | Invoice with new bank details | S, T | Code compares IBAN/BIC with the allowlisted beneficiary and blocks before Airwallex is called; Opus only explains; agents cannot change the allowlist | src/policy/fraud.ts, test/fraud.test.ts, npm run fraud\n2 | Fake supplier | Lookalike vendor name (one letter, a swap, Cyrillic letters) | S | Edit distance and a homoglyph skeleton against the allowlist; blocked | test/fraud.test.ts\n3 | Anyone who sends a document | Prompt injection (\"SYSTEM: ignore your rules\", \"pre-approved\", hidden characters) | T, E | Documents are wrapped as data; code flags planted lines; readings have no payee or approval field; Sonnet's invoice reading must match the document's own lines; payees come from the allowlist and the ledger | …"},
{"id":38,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Added since 30 October","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#added-since-30-october","text":"Rows 32 to 39 cover what was built after the 30 October review: the autonomous agents (D19, D22), origins (D24), the\nTAP plan (D25), test-money recycling, the contract and header checks of 2 November, and /try/sign (4 November). Row 31 (MFA sessions, D20) is\nabove.\n# | Attacker | Attack | STRIDE | What stops it | Proof\n32 | A world event or another agent's message that carries instructions (autonomous agents, D19 and D22) | Steer an agent into paying, raising its own limit, or skipping a check | T, E | An agent acts only through its tools, and each tool runs code's checks and then the rail's own limit (the mandate on chain, the card at Airwallex); messages between agents move no money (at most two per wake); a raise is a proposal for Face ID; the prompt and every tool result are redacted; the CFO's pause or idle switch stops the rest of a wake (finish aside) | src/agents/loop.ts, src/autonomy/runtime.ts, test/autonomy-runtime.test.ts, test/autonomy-blocked.test.ts, agents-autonomy-redteam.md\n33 | A runaway agent loop, or an agent that burns the model budget | Many payments, or a large Claude bill | E, D | Velocity limits (row 24); a Claude cost cap per agent per hour and per run, …"},
{"id":39,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Execution re-checks the signature (20 November, independent review)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#execution-re-checks-the-signature-20-november-independent-review","text":"An independent review found two weaknesses on the money path. Both are fixed, each with a test that failed before:\n\n- Finding 1 (high): execution trusted database rows, not signatures. The execution guard (beginExecution,\n src/policy/approvals.ts) compared the stored terms' hash with the hash on the approval row; both live in the same\n database. The reviewer wrote an approvals row with method passkey and no stored signature, set the proposal\n APPROVED, added an audit row through audit(), and the guard returned terms for EUR 9,999.00. Now, inside the same\n write lock, the guard re-verifies the approval (src/policy/signedApproval.ts): every stored passkey signature it\n counts must verify against the enrolled public key over the exact terms (challenge, origin, RP id, user present and\n verified, ES256 or RS256 signature: the checks verifyApprovalSignature makes, run synchronously by\n src/passkey/storedSignature.ts and held to the same answers by test/stored-signature.test.ts); as many different\n people as the approval names, and two people's whenever four eyes applies to the signed terms; a high-risk payment's security\n key too; a line of a signed batch through the batch's own …"},
{"id":40,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Outside audit: page integrity and credential changes (20 November)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#outside-audit-page-integrity-and-credential-changes-20-november","text":"- Finding 1.5, the approval page. The approval, enrolment and policy pages are each one document: script and\n stylesheet inline, under a CSP that allows exactly those two by SHA-256 (no 'self', no 'unsafe-inline'), so the\n served HTML is all that runs (src/approve/integrity.ts). npm run approval-page-record publishes each page's hash\n and CSP in evidence/approval-page.json, with Purser Cloud's console (nonces and the\n deployment's addresses set aside); each phone page shows its build id. npm run verify-approval-page -- \n fetches a live page from any machine and compares. The test fails when the record and the code differ. A lying page\n still cannot get a payment run on other terms: the runner and the engine verify the signature over their own\n canonical terms. Proof: test/approval-page-integrity.test.ts, test/browser/approve-design.check.ts.\n- Finding 1.3, a passkey written into the database. Before, it was enrolled. Now the enrolment ceremony seals each\n passkey: an HMAC of its id, public key, RP id, origin, person and enrolment time, with a key outside the ledger\n (PURSER_ENROLMENT_SEAL_KEY, or passkey-seal.key in the keys directory; src/passkey/seal.ts). …"},
{"id":41,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Agent cards frozen by default (19 November, fifth round)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#agent-cards-frozen-by-default-19-november-fifth-round","text":"Until the fifth round, an agent's card was ACTIVE at Airwallex all the time, bounded by its own limits and merchant\ncategories. A charge Airwallex approved on those limits that never reached the ledger (a merchant charging the card by\nitself, a leaked card number, a lost webhook and poll) was found afterwards by the reconciliation, not prevented: the\nred team's hidden-payment was the last attack \"found afterwards\". Now:\n\n- Frozen at rest. Every agent card (our three agents' and each outside agent's) is INACTIVE at Airwallex. A new\n card is frozen right after it is issued, and the runner's card sync keeps it so (wantCardStatus,\n src/policy/cards.ts).\n- Thawed for one approved purchase. Purser opens a window only for a purchase it approved under the policy (an\n agent's plan purchase, an outside agent's payment after its own checks and the spend hold, a renewal a scene expects).\n The window is recorded in the audit log (card.window_opened: agent, merchant, amount, until), so the runner in\n another process leaves the card thawed while it is open. No window opens while the policy has the card frozen\n (emergency stop, pause, velocity stop, revoked agent). …"},
{"id":42,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Signed audit checkpoints (20 November, outside audit 1.4)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#signed-audit-checkpoints-20-november-outside-audit-14","text":"The outside audit's finding 1.4: the audit log is hash-chained, but its anchors are unsigned, so whoever can write the\nSQLite file can append rows after the last published anchor, or rewrite the chain and recompute every hash. The chain's\nown check (npm run verify, the gate before a payment) cannot see either: what is left verifies. Exercised on 20\nNovember on a runner's ledger file, through the runner's own code (checkpoint drill:\n56 of 56 steps; six attacks each refused before a payment, a loosening policy change and a key enrolment, and found by\nnpm run verify-audit). No standing runner has it switched on yet, and Purser Cloud's hosted engine (Durable Objects)\ndoes not run it. The key is a file on the runner, not in a KMS or an HSM.\n\n- A checkpoint is one JSON line: its own number n, the rows it covers (entries), the head hash (row_hash of\n the last of them), the time, the key id and public key, and the id of the checkpoint before (prev), signed with\n Ed25519 (src/audit/checkpoint.ts). The lines go to an append-only file (PURSER_CHECKPOINT_FILE, by default\n .checkpoints.jsonl), so the checkpoints are a chain of their own.\n- The key is not in the ledger. …"},
{"id":43,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Purser Cloud's emergency stop, and the proof bundles fuzzed again (26 November)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#purser-clouds-emergency-stop-and-the-proof-bundles-fuzzed-again-26-november","text":"Row 19's emergency stop held on the runner only. A company's engine in Purser Cloud (one Durable Object per company,\ncloud/src/engine/) ran the same payment executors, which already ask the stop before and during every payment, but\nnothing in the Cloud could pull it: someone who saw an agent misbehave in a Cloud company could reject proposals one by\none, not stop them all. Now:\n\n- One stop, the runner's. It is the same CFO policy setting (freeze), changed by the same policy change\n (src/policy/emergencyStop.ts, src/executors/policyChange.ts): POST /v1/engine/emergency-stop with { on: true }\n or { on: false }, from a signed-in session only (a key gets 403), files it, and nothing changes until the CFO\n approves it with the passkey (POST /v1/engine/proposals/{id}/approve: the signature over its exact terms, and a new\n key's cooling-off, as for a payment). Lifting it loosens the policy, so it is signed the same way. Both are\n policy.changed rows in the company's audit log, shown in its events and GET /v1/engine (emergency_stop: { on,\n since, proposal_id }), and told to every owner (emergency_stop.requested, .on, .lift_requested, .lifted).\n- What it stops. …"},
{"id":44,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Approval notifications in Slack or Teams, Face ID kept (26 November)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#approval-notifications-in-slack-or-teams-face-id-kept-26-november","text":"The runner can tell a Slack or Microsoft Teams channel that a payment or a policy change waits for the CFO\n(src/integrations/approvalNotify.ts, hooked where the runner syncs the waiting proposals to the relay). A chat\nmessage is outside Purser's trust boundary, so:\n\n- It never approves. One deep link to the passkey approval page (/approve/ on the relay), with no query or\n fragment (no viewer key, no token); no button that acts, no reply word. A Teams card's only action is OpenUrl.\n- The webhook URL is a credential. Read from PURSER_NOTIFY_SLACK_WEBHOOK / PURSER_NOTIFY_TEAMS_WEBHOOK only,\n off when unset; never logged, never in the audit trail (notify.sent / notify.failed rows hold the channel, the\n HTTP status and the attempts), never in an error. Hosts allowed: hooks.slack.com (https, port 443); Teams'\n *.webhook.office.com or a Power Automate workflow's host (*.logic.azure.com, *.environment.api.powerplatform.com).\n Any other URL is refused at start and that channel stays off.\n- No injection from a payee's name. …"},
{"id":45,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Security headers and rate limits (checked 2 November)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#security-headers-and-rate-limits-checked-2-november","text":"Read from the code that serves each answer and asserted in test/security-headers.test.ts.\nWhere | Headers | Finding\nRelay Worker pages (worker/src/core.ts pageResponse) and the 404 | A CSP per page from src/relay/assets.ts (default-src 'none', script and style by hash or 'self', never 'unsafe-inline', frame-ancestors 'none', base-uri 'none'), HSTS (max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains), x-frame-options: DENY, nosniff, no-referrer, no-store, cross-origin-opener-policy: same-origin, a permissions policy (passkeys for this site only; no camera, microphone, location, payment sheet or USB), x-robots-tag | 6 November (A3): the 404 lacked the permissions policy and the opener policy, /favicon.ico was a 404, and Firefox logged a CSP error for the icon it fetches by itself on /policy, /approve and /metal/report (img-src 'none'); fixed: the 404 is built like a page, /favicon.ico serves Purser's mark, those pages name it and allow img-src 'self'. Live only after npm run relay:deploy (Max). …"},
{"id":46,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Limits on every external call","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#limits-on-every-external-call","text":"Call | Timeout | Retries | When the answer is lost\nAirwallex API | 30 s | up to 4 with backoff on 429 (nothing was done); GET also on a network error; one call per 200 ms (half the sandbox limit) | a POST without an answer is never resent: it becomes \"ambiguous\" and is resolved by its request_id\nAlta RPC | 15 s | none | the step fails and is re-run from the ledger\nx402 paid request | 60 s | none | if signed, \"in doubt\": looked up by its nonce on the facilitator, never paid twice\nFacilitator settlements, x402 offers | 15 s | none | the step fails safely\nClaude (all three models) | 180 s | 2 (SDK) | the deterministic parser decides\nRelay sync | 20 s | the next sync | verdicts are kept and sent with the next sync\nmetal-agent CLI | 180 s | none | an error: line is an error, never a refusal\nIdempotency keys:\n- x402 settlement ids;\n- refund payment ids (refund-);\n- sweep ids;\n- Airwallex request_id for every conversion and transfer;\n- a single-use FX quote;\n- one live payout per invoice;\n- one credit per on-chain transfer."},
{"id":47,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Least privilege","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#least-privilege","text":"- Agents: each agent has its own on-chain mandate, with a per-payment cap, a total budget, a single payee and an\n expiry, and holds only its own mandate key. The CFO policy can only be stricter.\n- Each agent's tools (25 November): every agent principal lists exactly the tools it may call and the money actions\n it may take; anything else is refused in code before it runs and audited (principal.tool_refused). The table, held\n to the code by test/agent-permissions.test.ts: security/agent-permissions.md.\n- Know your agent (26 November): each agent principal has its own Ed25519 signing key (the ledger keeps the public\n half). A request to the agent API carries a signature over its tool, its body, its time and a nonce, so it can be\n attributed to one agent key, and a replay is refused (principal.identity_refused, with a reason code). The money\n action records the key id. Required on the runner's agent API (npm run mcp) by default; PURSER_AGENT_IDENTITY can relax it:\n security/agent-identity.md. …"},
{"id":48,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: If the approver is unavailable","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#if-the-approver-is-unavailable","text":"1. Away or out of reach: nothing above the limits is paid. The payment waits for the signature and expires unsigned; payments inside the limits go on. (src/policy/approvals.ts)\n2. No deputy, no delegation: neither is built. A second person can be enrolled beforehand; where four eyes does not apply either passkey approves, where it applies both must sign. Our runs had one person: the second signature came from a test passkey. (src/policy/fourEyes.ts; npm run passkey -- add )\n3. A lost phone: the passkey is replaced, not recovered. The old one counts until the new one is confirmed, and is revoked then. (src/passkey/ledger.ts)\n4. Who may enrol a new passkey, on the runner: only the person at the runner, who opens a ten-minute window with a one-time code and confirms the new passkey's fingerprint. (npm run relay -- --enrol --replace, then npm run passkey -- confirm)\n5. Who may enrol, in Purser Cloud (built, not live): a signed-in owner or an API key with the admin scope starts a person's enrolment; an owner's passkey, once any owner has one, only a signed-in owner. …"},
{"id":49,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Accepted risks and what is out of scope","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#accepted-risks-and-what-is-out-of-scope","text":"- zod advisory (fixed 2026-10-29). @x402/* is at 2.29.0, which uses fixed zod 4, and an override gives\n @metalntwx/metal-agent zod 4.6.7 as well. npm audit reports 0 vulnerabilities. A live npm run verify (21 checks,\n through metal-agent) and an x402 sale refused by policy behaved as before.\n- The relay serves the phone's script. A compromised Worker or Cloudflare account can serve a script that\n shows one thing and asks Face ID to sign another waiting proposal's hash. The runner key and its signatures cannot\n stop a lying script; only a page not served by the relay could (a native app).\n What still holds:\n - the runner executes only waiting proposals' exact terms, so payees come from the allowlist and amounts are\n built by code;\n - the phone can only tighten the CFO policy, and the runner enforces that (any loosening is proposed on the\n runner);\n - every approval is in the audit report.\n With passkey owners on (block 1, KIT11_PASSKEY_OWNERS=on) this no longer holds for the passkey-owned account\n (security review, 1 November). The two passkeys are that account's on-chain owners, and the system prompt for Face\n ID shows the site, never the challenge. …"},
{"id":50,"doc":"docs/security.md","title":"Security and threat model: Checks","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/security.md#checks","text":"- npm test: the full suite, including test/adversarial.test.ts. CI runs it on every push, with type checks,\n gitleaks on the pushed commits and the whole history of the branch under check, and npm audit for the root and\n worker/.\n- npm run redteam: 35 scripted attacks plus documents Claude Opus writes as the attacker, each in a fresh\n throwaway world, through the code the runner runs; every attack must fail (report in docs/redteam/report.json,\n shown on the landing).\n- npm run zero-trust: the zero-trust matrix, every attack against the real code with the rails stood in, and its\n report (zero-trust.md); with -- --check it writes nothing and fails when the committed report\n differs. The matrix also runs in npm test.\n- npm run evals: the agents' eval set (normal, too expensive, fraud, injection, double payment, price notice)\n with the real models; CI runs the same cases with the parsers.\n- npm run reconcile: the ledger against Airwallex and Alta; the runner does it a minute after start, then daily.\n- npm run verify: re-checks the chain, the mandates, the Airwallex records and every passkey signature, offline\n where it can. …"},
{"id":51,"doc":"docs/fraud-and-injection.md","title":"Fraud and prompt injection: Invoice fraud and prompt injection","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/fraud-and-injection.md#invoice-fraud-and-prompt-injection","text":"How code stops a changed IBAN, a lookalike supplier and a planted instruction before anything is signed.\n\nMoved from the project README. Back to the README."},
{"id":52,"doc":"docs/fraud-and-injection.md","title":"Fraud and prompt injection: Invoice fraud","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/fraud-and-injection.md#invoice-fraud","text":"Business email compromise is the classic way to steal a B2B payment: an invoice that looks like the supplier's\nannounces new bank details, or comes from a name one letter off. Here code checks, from the ledger, before\nAirwallex is called (src/policy/fraud.ts):\n\n- Changed bank details: the invoice's IBAN or BIC differs from the allowlisted beneficiary's.\n- Lookalike vendor: the name is not the allowlisted one but close to it (one or two letters, a swap, or the same\n letters from another alphabet, such as a Cyrillic \"е\"). Its bank details are compared with the supplier it\n pretends to be.\n- Another account holder: the \"Account name\" on the invoice is not the supplier.\n- Evidence, never the reason on its own: wording that announces a bank change or pushes for speed.\n\nA blocked invoice reads no balance, asks for no quote and creates no proposal; it is audited as\ninvoice.fraud_suspected with every signal, and shows on the dashboard as \"Invoice blocked: possible fraud\".\nOpus then explains it to the CFO and lists how to verify it through a channel the invoice did not supply; its\nanswer can only be \"do not pay\" or \"verify first\", and the block stands either way. …"},
{"id":53,"doc":"docs/fraud-and-injection.md","title":"Fraud and prompt injection: Prompt injection","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/fraud-and-injection.md#prompt-injection","text":"Documents are data. Every incoming document is screened by code first (src/policy/injection.ts) for lines aimed\nat a machine: orders to the AI (\"SYSTEM: ignore your rules…\"), claims that approval is not needed (\"pre-approved by\nthe CFO\", \"skip the approval step\"), and hidden characters (zero-width or bidirectional controls). What it finds is\nlogged as document.injection_flagged and shown on the dashboard as \"Planted instruction ignored\". It changes\nnothing, because nothing a model says can approve or move money:\n\n- The models read inside ` tags, told that the content is from an outside party and never an instruction.\n- Their readings have no field for a payee or an approval. Where code can read the document's own lines, Sonnet's\n invoice reading must agree with them on number, vendor, amount, currency, IBAN and BIC, or code uses those lines\n instead (claude.rejected). Payees come from the allowlist, refund addresses from the ledger.\n- Opus only writes advice beside a proposal. Only Max's passkey (or their typed hash) approves, and the executor runs\n only the approved hash. …"},
{"id":54,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: Connect Purser to anything","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#connect-purser-to-anything","text":"Every way into Purser and out of it, on one page: the payment rails, AI agents over MCP, the API and its webhooks,\nno-code tools, accounting packages, Peppol, ISO 20022, chat and the full export. Each has its honest label, a quickstart\nof a line or two and a link to its guide. Purser Cloud shows the same list (its Connections page), read from\nGET /v1/connections (cloud/src/connections.ts), and test/connections-hub.test.ts holds this page to it.\n\nThe rule behind all of them. An agent or an integration may read and propose. Only the CFO's passkey\napproves money: a signed-in person in Purser Cloud signs the exact terms: one changed cent and the approval no longer matches the terms. No\nkey, agent, integration, webhook or chat message can approve. The approve route refuses every API key\n(POST /v1/engine/proposals/{id}/approve needs a signed-in person's session). If the CFO set a pay-alone limit\n(ap.alone_eur, off unless set), a proposal within it is paid under the CFO's own policy, and the answer says so in\nalone. Test money only until a company goes live.\n\nThe labels. live: built, and running in Purser Cloud. …"},
{"id":55,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: At a glance","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#at-a-glance","text":"The sponsors' services are the money rails (Airwallex, Alta (formerly Metal), Visa through Airwallex's Airi) and the\nmodel (Claude, by Anthropic). Everything else on this page connects to Purser itself: it reads, proposes, receives the\nbooks or carries a message, and none of it moves money."},
{"id":56,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: The active stack","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#the-active-stack","text":"Six services, each with a dated run on record (the proof is in the table below). Everything else on this page is built\nor planned and not active yet: it joins the stack once it has run live against the real service.\n\nEach mark is the file on record, unchanged: sources and hashes in src/ui/logos/README.md\nand docs/assets/logos/SOURCES.md; permissions in\nlogo-permissions.md. Visa and T:0 are named in text. A mark names a service Purser\nconnects to: never \"certified\", \"endorsed\", \"approved by\" or \"partner of\"."},
{"id":57,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: Where each one stands","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#where-each-one-stands","text":"The labels in the tables further down are the catalogue's. This table adds one stricter question: is there a dated\nrun on record?\nBadge | Means | Ran against the real service (or its sandbox or testnet), with a dated record linked. | Code done and tested against stand-ins; waits for credentials or a first recorded run. | Code exists, but a named piece is missing. | Named only; nothing built yet.\nPartner | Status | Catalogue label | Proof, or what is missing\nAirwallex | | sandbox | Soak, 20 Nov: 30 supplier payments, 5 negative controls refused; API coverage, 19 Nov. Check: npm run health.\nAlta (testnet) | | testnet | Series, 19 Nov: 21 mandate-checked payments, 3 refused on chain; refusals, 20 Nov. Check: npm run health.\nVisa via Airwallex Airi | | sandbox | vic-5, 14 Nov: Airi's test card, terms hash read back, credential reuse refused. Check: npm run airi:vic-5 -- --dry.\nClaude (MCP connector) | | live | Added in the Claude iOS app on 13 Nov (how it was verified).\nClaude (models in Purser) | | not a catalogue row | Payables agents' evals, 20 Nov: Haiku, Sonnet and Opus, 62 of 62 cases each. …"},
{"id":58,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: How it fits together","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#how-it-fits-together","text":"No arrow from an agent, a key or an integration reaches a rail without passing Purser's policy, and above the limit only\nthe CFO's passkey opens it (the rule)."},
{"id":59,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: Connect in 5 minutes","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#connect-in-5-minutes","text":"Sandbox, testnet and test cards only: no real card, no real money. Keys go into the environment (a runner's .env, which\ngit ignores) or into a Worker as a secret, from worker/: npx wrangler secret put --config \n(the prompt asks for the value). Never into git, code or a chat.\n\n#### Airwallex\n\n1. Open a sandbox account (Airwallex's sandbox guide (https://www.airwallex.com/docs/developer-tools/sandbox-environment/sandbox-environment-overview)).\n2. In the sandbox web app, make a scoped API key: Read or Write per resource, no more than the scoped key lists.\n3. Set AIRWALLEX_CLIENT_ID and AIRWALLEX_API_KEY in the runner's environment.\n4. npm run health. Working: ok airwallex sandbox: EUR … (the balances). The whole story: run-it.md.\n\n#### Alta (formerly Metal)\n\n1. In the Alta testnet console (https://console-testnet.metalntwx.com), make an RPC endpoint; fund test accounts from\n the faucet (Alta's guide (https://docs.metalntwx.com/build/prepare/fund-a-test-account)).\n2. Set METAL_RPC_URL (the URL is the credential) and METAL_ENDPOINT_SECRET.\n3. npm run health. Working: ok metal chain id: 63825, ok metal finality, ok x402 facilitator: ready.\n4. Mandates and payments: metal-award.md. …"},
{"id":60,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: Payment rails","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#payment-rails","text":"Money moves only on these, and only within the limits the CFO signed or after the CFO's Face ID on the exact terms. T:0\nis an outside ledger in the same group: it receives the books and moves no money. The services are named as the ones\nPurser calls; no endorsement implied.\nConnection | Label | Quickstart | Guide\nAirwallex | sandbox | Sandbox keys in the runner's environment (AIRWALLEX_CLIENT_ID, AIRWALLEX_API_KEY); npm run health checks them, and run-it.md runs the whole story. | airwallex.md\nAlta (formerly Metal) | testnet | An Alta testnet RPC from the Alta console in METAL_RPC_URL; npm run health checks it. A mandate per agent on chain, x402 payments. | metal-award.md\nVisa via Airwallex Airi | sandbox | npm run airi:vic-5 -- --dry runs the flow on labelled stand-ins with no network; preflight and live need KIT11_AIRI_RAIL=on, the Airwallex sandbox keys and Airi. | visa-award.md\nT:0 (outside ledger) | sandbox | T0_API_KEY in the environment, then npm run t0 -- push --rate USD=0.92 --dry-run, then without --dry-run. | t0.md"},
{"id":61,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: AI agents over MCP","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#ai-agents-over-mcp","text":"One remote MCP server per Purser Cloud, at /mcp: 14 read tools, resources and prompts; with a token made to propose,\nit can file a payment for the CFO. No tool approves or pays. Each client's exact config for your cloud's address is on\nits /connect-ai page.\nConnection | Label | Quickstart | Guide\nMCP server (Connect any AI) | live | Add https:///mcp to any client that speaks MCP over HTTP; sign in with a connector token (Connections, Connect your AI) or the demo company's purser-demo-read-only. | connect-any-ai.md\nClaude | live | claude.ai or the Claude apps: Settings, Connectors, Add custom connector, paste the /mcp address. Claude Code: claude mcp add --transport http purser /mcp. | connect-claude.md\nChatGPT | built, not tested live | Apps, +, Add custom MCP server, URL /mcp, authentication OAuth. | connect-claude.md\nCursor | built, not tested live | The Add to Cursor link on /connect-ai, or .cursor/mcp.json. | connect-claude.md\nVS Code | built, not tested live | The Add to VS Code link on /connect-ai, or MCP: Add Server, HTTP. …"},
{"id":62,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: The API and webhooks","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#the-api-and-webhooks","text":"Connection | Label | Quickstart | Guide\nRead API (REST) and its OpenAPI | live | curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $PURSER_API_KEY\" https:///v1/invoices; the document at /v1/openapi.json (the read part at /v1/openapi.read.json). | REST and OpenAPI, connections.md\nWebhooks | live | POST /v1/webhook { \"url\": \"https://…\" } as an owner; check x-purser-signature (HMAC-SHA256 of t.body) on every event. | connections.md\nTypeScript and Python SDKs | built, not tested live | Purser.fromEnv() (PURSER_URL, PURSER_API_KEY), then proposePayment(\"AP-0004\"); no approve method. | TypeScript, Python\nA2A Agent Card | built, not tested live | curl https:///.well-known/agent.json: skills that read or propose, for discovery. | A2A Agent Card"},
{"id":63,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: No-code tools","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#no-code-tools","text":"Through the API and the signed webhook, with the plain HTTP modules every tool has. Nothing here is a published Zapier\nor Make app.\nConnection | Label | Quickstart | Guide\nZapier and Make (HTTP modules) | built, not tested live | GET https:///v1/engine/invoices, then POST /v1/engine/invoices/{id}/pay with a read+propose key; trigger on Purser's webhook (*Catch Hook*, *Custom webhook*). Written from the OpenAPI document; not run in Zapier or Make. | no-code.md\nn8n node | built, not tested live | cd integrations/n8n && npm install && npm run build, link the folder into n8n, credential: your cloud's URL and a read+propose key. Not yet built or published from here. | n8n"},
{"id":64,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: Accounting","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#accounting","text":"Connection | Label | Quickstart | Guide\nXero | format export | GET /v1/export/csv/xero/bills or /journals with a read key; import the file in Xero. | connections.md\nXero (API) | built, not tested live | With the owner's Xero OAuth app: npx tsx src/cli/workplace.ts xero-tenants, then books xero --dry-run. | workplace.md\nQuickBooks Online | format export | GET /v1/export/csv/quickbooks/bills; QuickBooks maps the columns at import. No journals yet. | connections.md\nExact Online (CSV) | format export | GET /v1/export/csv/exact/bills or /journals: Exact's own import templates. | connections.md\nXero bills (connected in Purser Cloud) | built, not tested live | Each company: Connections, Connect Xero, pick its organisation; then Send bills to Xero (drafts). Drafts only, never authorised or paid in Xero. | owner-setup.md\nQuickBooks Online (API) | built, not tested live | Each company: Connections, Connect QuickBooks. Connect flow only; sending bills is planned. | quickbooks-plan.md\nExact Online (API) | built, not tested live | Each company: Connections, Connect Exact Online; its runner sets ERP_EXACT_OAUTH=on. …"},
{"id":65,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: Peppol, ISO 20022, chat, workplace and the full export","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#peppol-iso-20022-chat-workplace-and-the-full-export","text":"Connection | Label | Quickstart | Guide\nPeppol invoices (UBL, BIS Billing 3.0) | built, not tested live | npm run peppol:check -- reads a file and names each rule broken; npm run payables -- add files it in the payables inbox, checked like a PDF. | peppol.md\nPeppol network (an Access Point) | planned | Receiving over the network needs a certified Access Point, the owner's choice and registration; nothing is wired yet. | peppol.md\nISO 20022 pacs.008 | format export | npm run iso20022 writes a pacs.008.001.08 message for one paid invoice, validated against the official schema. | connections.md\nSlack and Microsoft Teams messages | built, not tested live | Each company: Connections, Slack and Teams, paste its own Slack incoming webhook or Teams Workflow URL, Send a test. approval.needed, payment.paid and books.closed then post there; no real channel has received one yet. | connections.md\nInvoices by e-mail (forwarded from Gmail or Outlook) | built, not tested live | Forward supplier invoices to the company's Purser address (Settings, Company, Inbox); Gmail's confirmation code shows in Settings. No mail domain is routed yet. …"},
{"id":66,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: Build your own connector","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#build-your-own-connector","text":"Four things are enough for anything not listed above.\n\n1. A key with the scopes read and propose. An owner makes it in Purser Cloud (Settings, API keys, \"read and\n propose\"); it is shown once. Send it as Authorization: Bearer . Use read alone if the connector only reads;\n never give it admin.\n2. The OpenAPI document. https:///v1/openapi.json (everything) or /v1/openapi.read.json (the read API\n alone); in the repository, openapi/purser.yaml. Each operation names the scope it\n needs (x-purser-needs). Proposing is POST /v1/engine/invoices/{id}/pay; no scope approves.\n3. The webhook signature. Every event carries x-purser-signature: t=,v1=. Compute\n HMAC-SHA256 under your webhook's secret over ` ${t}.${raw body} , compare it with v1 in constant time, and\n refuse a t older than a few minutes. Then read the invoice or proposal again with your key before acting: an\n event is a nudge, never the truth.\n4. The MCP endpoint. https:///mcp for an AI client, with a connector token (Connections, Connect your AI) or\n OAuth 2.1. A connector token works at /mcp` only."},
{"id":67,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: Keys and scopes","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#keys-and-scopes","text":"Keys. An owner makes a key in Purser Cloud (Settings, API keys, \"read and propose\"), or with\nPOST /v1/keys { \"name\": \"…\", \"scopes\": [\"read\", \"propose\"] } from their signed-in session. The key is shown once,\nexpires (90 days by default) and can be revoked. Keep it in the environment (PURSER_API_KEY), never in code. Scopes:\nScope | What it may do\nread | Read invoices, documents, suppliers, payments, the transactions register, the ledger and its reports.\npropose | File an invoice's payment for the CFO's approval (POST /v1/engine/invoices/{id}/pay). Nothing more.\nadmin | Manage the company (keys, people, settings). It covers propose. An integration should not hold it.\nsync | The company's own runner pushing its records. Not for integrations.\napprove | Never a key's. A signed-in CFO's (or, in a company with no CFO, an owner's): approve or reject with their own passkey. admin does not cover it. Roles: security/roles.md.\nStatus of the sections below: the SDKs, the A2A card, the n8n node, the no-code recipes and the approval notifications are\nbuilt and tested locally (see \"Tests\" at the end). None of them has been used live by an outside agent or a no-code tool\nyet."},
{"id":68,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: MCP (Claude and other AI clients)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#mcp-claude-and-other-ai-clients","text":"Safety boundary: the read tools always; propose_invoice_payment and payment_proposal only with a token made to\npropose. No tool approves or pays. A connector token works at /mcp only. Details:\nmcp.md, connect-claude.md and connect-any-ai.md."},
{"id":69,"doc":"docs/integrations/README.md","title":"Integrations: REST and OpenAPI","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/integrations/README.md#rest-and-openapi","text":"The API as OpenAPI 3.1: openapi/purser.yaml, and served at /openapi.json (also\n/v1/openapi.json; the read-only part at /v1/openapi.read.json). The reference page is /api: the same document as\none HTML page, with no script and no third-party asset. npm run openapi writes the YAML from the route table\n(cloud/src/app.ts) and the zod schemas its routes parse bodies with, and test/openapi-spec.test.ts fails when a\nroute is in the code but not in the document, or the other way round, or when the file is out of date.\n\nSafety boundary: each operation names the scope it needs (x-purser-needs). Proposing needs propose. Approving needs\napprove, which no key can hold: a signed-in CFO's own passkey over the exact terms."},
{"id":70,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: Connect any AI to Purser","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#connect-any-ai-to-purser","text":"Use your own AI assistant with your company's Purser: Claude (claude.ai, the Claude apps, Claude Code), ChatGPT, Cursor,\nVS Code's agent mode, Gemini CLI, Windsurf, or any client that speaks the Model Context Protocol (MCP) to a remote server. It reads\nyour books, and you can let it propose an invoice's payment. It can never approve or pay. Every payment still needs\nthe CFO's Face ID in Purser Cloud: the approval is a passkey signature over the payment's exact terms, and no token can\nmake one.\n\nPurser is a remote MCP server (Streamable HTTP) at /mcp. For the hosted test cloud\nthat is https://purser-try.max-31b.workers.dev/mcp.\n\nWhat ran live, and where. On 13 November 2026, 06:57 UTC, tools/list there with the demo company's token answered\nthe 7 read tools of the version deployed then (this version has 15; see *Which clients were verified*). The same morning the owner added Purser as a connector in the Claude iOS app: its 7 tools showed,\nand agent_decisions answered through that connector. …"},
{"id":71,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: Three steps","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#three-steps","text":"1. Make a connector token. In Purser Cloud go to Connections, Connect your AI. Name the token. Tick *may propose\n payments* only if your AI should file payments for approval. Click Make a token and copy it: it is shown once.\n Only an owner, signed in with a passkey, can make or revoke a token.\n To try first, use the demo company's public token instead: purser-demo-read-only (read only, made-up data).\n2. Add Purser to your AI, as its section below shows: the /mcp address, and either the token as an\n Authorization: Bearer header or the client's own sign-in.\n3. Sign in where the client asks: Purser's consent page takes your token, or Use the demo company.\n\nThen ask: \"what needs my Face ID?\", \"show me this quarter's VAT\", \"explain the Lagerhaus payment\" or \"what did my agents\ndecide this week?\". Purser also offers five ready-made prompts (below)."},
{"id":72,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: Claude","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#claude","text":"- claude.ai, the Claude desktop and mobile apps (tested live in the iOS app on 13 Nov): Settings,\n Connectors, Add custom connector, paste the /mcp address. Claude opens Purser's consent page: paste your token, or\n choose Use the demo company.\n- Claude Code:\n claude mcp add --transport http purser /mcp --header \"Authorization: Bearer \",\n or the plugin below."},
{"id":73,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: The connect page","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#the-connect-page","text":"Every Purser Cloud serves /connect-ai (on the test cloud:\npurser-try.max-31b.workers.dev/connect-ai (https://purser-try.max-31b.workers.dev/connect-ai), once this version is\ndeployed): a tab per client with the exact config for that cloud's address, and a one-click Add to Cursor and\nAdd to VS Code link. The tabs below say the same."},
{"id":74,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: ChatGPT","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#chatgpt","text":"In ChatGPT on the web: Apps (or Plugins), +, Add custom MCP server; name Purser, URL /mcp,\nauthentication OAuth. ChatGPT finds Purser's sign-in itself and registers by Client ID Metadata Document (or\ndynamic registration); on Purser's page paste your connector token or choose Use the demo company. ChatGPT cannot send\na fixed token, so the demo token does not apply there. OpenAI's pages (read 13 Nov) list custom MCP servers for\nBusiness, Enterprise and Edu workspaces, and read/fetch connectors for Pro. Purser's tools are all read-only, and\nsearch/fetch tools are no longer required."},
{"id":75,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: Cursor","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#cursor","text":"~/.cursor/mcp.json (every project) or .cursor/mcp.json (one project), or the Add to Cursor link on /connect-ai\n(cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/mcp/install?name=purser&config=/mcp\"}>). Without a\nheader Cursor signs in through Purser's page."},
{"id":76,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: VS Code (GitHub Copilot agent mode)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#vs-code-github-copilot-agent-mode","text":"The Add to VS Code link on /connect-ai (vscode:mcp/install?, opened\nthrough https://vscode.dev/redirect), or Command Palette, MCP: Add Server, HTTP. VS Code's documentation now\nputs new servers in .mcp.json at the workspace root (or ~/.copilot/mcp-config.json):\n\nThe older .vscode/mcp.json (\"servers\", with an inputs prompt for the token) still works; /connect-ai shows both."},
{"id":77,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: Windsurf (now Devin Desktop)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#windsurf-now-devin-desktop","text":"Windsurf's MCP documentation now lives in Devin's docs. In ~/.config/devin/mcp_config.json (older Windsurf:\n~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json), serverUrl (or url) and headers:"},
{"id":78,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: Which clients were verified, and how","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#which-clients-were-verified-and-how","text":"Client | How it was checked (13 Nov 2026)\nMCP Inspector 2.15.0 (CLI) | Run on 13 Nov on a local cloud (npm run mcp:local): tools/list (14 tools then, --strict: no schema-portability warnings), tools/call, resources/list, resources/read, resources/templates/list, prompts/list\nThe official MCP TypeScript SDK client (1.32) | Run in test/browser/connector.check.ts: OAuth sign-in in a real browser, then every read tool and a prompt\nClaude iOS app | Run by the owner on 13 Nov against the deployed cloud before this version (7 tools then)\nclaude.ai, Claude Desktop, Claude Code | From Claude's help centre and Claude Code's docs (custom connectors, claude mcp add --transport http, DCR and CIMD)\nChatGPT | From OpenAI's developer docs (custom MCP server, OAuth with PKCE, CIMD/DCR, no static tokens)\nCursor | From cursor.com/docs/mcp and its install-link page\nVS Code / Copilot | From VS Code's MCP configuration reference and its install-link guide\nGemini CLI | From the Gemini CLI MCP docs (httpUrl, gemini mcp add)\nWindsurf / Devin | From Devin's docs (Cascade MCP, serverUrl)\nThe protocol itself, both eras, is checked in test/mcp-upgrade.test.ts against the 2026-07-28 specification."},
{"id":79,"doc":"docs/connect-claude.md","title":"Connect Claude: What your AI can do","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/connect-claude.md#what-your-ai-can-do","text":"Each tool's annotations, the resources, the prompts and the error codes are in the reference, mcp.md.\nTool | What it does | Needs\ncompany_overview | Money in and out, net cash, invoices by state, spend by agent, the newest decisions | any token\nlist_invoices, get_invoice | Supplier invoices, their checks and earlier versions | any token\nlist_transactions | Every money movement on every rail, with its approval, booking and proof | any token\nbooks_report | P&L, balance sheet, trial balance, VAT per quarter, payables, receivables | any token\nagent_decisions | The audit trail in words: who decided what (an agent, the CFO, or Purser's code) | any token\nwhat_needs_attention | Open, due, overdue, waiting, blocked | any token\ncash_position | Net cash (money in minus out since the first movement, not a bank balance) and a week-by-week projection from the books' due days | any token\npending_approvals | Invoices and proposals waiting for the CFO's Face ID, each with a link to approve it in Purser Cloud (read only) | any token\ncfo_policy | The rules every payment is held to, in plain words; the policy version in force; each agent's card limits; treasury settings | any token\nspend_breakdown | …"},
{"id":80,"doc":"docs/ask-purser.md","title":"Task cards (one sentence, one card): Task cards: a card for one task, from one sentence","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/ask-purser.md#task-cards-a-card-for-one-task-from-one-sentence","text":"Until 21 November this feature was called \"Ask Purser\"; that name is now the chat on Purser Cloud (/ask,\ncloud/src/ask/), so the feature is called task cards here. The code keeps its old names (src/agents/askPurser.ts,\nnpm run ask).\n\nThe CFO types on the runner, or on the phone (CFO policy page, \"Task card\"):\n\nTyped at the runner, up to the CFO policy's threshold for task cards (approval.task_card_eur, 300.00 to start;\nraising it needs Face ID), Purser issues the card at once, at most three a day, never above the four-eyes threshold,\nand only when the amount is written next to € or EUR and the date, if any, is in the message: *\"Done, within your policy: a single-use flight card •••• 4821, at most 250.00 EUR,\nuntil 2026-11-12.\"* Anything else, and every message sent from the phone or the viewer link (the relay cannot tell who holds the link)\nor by an outside agent, Purser proposes, with who asked in the signed terms: \"I proposed P-0011: … Approve it with Face ID and I book it.\",\nand Opus writes a short risk review beside the proposal. Either way Airwallex issues a virtual card that can pay\none airline charge, up to the amount, until the end of the day named. …"},
{"id":81,"doc":"docs/ask-purser.md","title":"Task cards (one sentence, one card): What decides what","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/ask-purser.md#what-decides-what","text":"Step | Who | What\nScreen the message | code (src/policy/injection.ts) | Instructions aimed at the AI (\"ignore your rules\", \"pre-approved\") or hidden characters: refused whole, before any model reads it\nRead the message | Claude Sonnet 5.5, or the plain parser without a key | Kind, amount as written, purpose, date\nDecide | code (planTask, src/agents/askPurser.ts) | Only flights (merchant category 4511, at most 1,500.00), hotels (7011, 1,000.00) and trains (4112, 500.00); the amount must be in the CFO's own words; the date at most 30 days ahead (7 days when none is named)\nApprove | at the runner, the CFO policy up to its threshold; otherwise the CFO, Face ID (two people above the four-eyes threshold), with Opus's review beside the terms | The exact card: kind, categories, amount, end, single use, and the hash of the message\nIssue | Airwallex Issuing | allowed_transaction_count: SINGLE, the categories, euros only, active_to; read back, and frozen if it differs from what was approved\nPay | the merchant, through Airwallex | One successful charge; anything else is declined by Airwallex\nAn agent can ask too: outside agents through the MCP tool ask_for_task_card. …"},
{"id":82,"doc":"docs/ask-purser.md","title":"Task cards (one sentence, one card): What is simulated","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/ask-purser.md#what-is-simulated","text":"The airline's charge is Airwallex's sandbox simulation (POST /simulation/issuing/create); no real flight is booked.\nSingle-use cards are documented by Airwallex (\"only 1 successful debit transaction\") and checked live in the sandbox\non 30 October (run log): SINGLE is accepted and reads back; after the one purchase\nAirwallex closes the card itself, a moment later, and declines a second charge with CARD_CLOSED. Purser freezes the\ncard if it is still open and otherwise records it closed."},
{"id":83,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Business model: a hypothesis","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#business-model-a-hypothesis","text":"Everything on this page is a hypothesis.\nNot validated with customers yet: 2 finance conversations (a CFO and a bank finance professional, quoted, anonymous); more in progress; no pilots, no revenue.\nNo letters of intent. The buyer, the channel and the price below are what we would test first, not what we have found. Outside facts carry a source we opened on the date given.\n\nBack to the business case index. The problem it answers: problem.md."},
{"id":84,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Who buys and who uses it (hypothesis)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#who-buys-and-who-uses-it-hypothesis","text":"Role | Who (hypothesis) | What they would need from Purser (hypothesis)\nBuyer | The finance team of an SMB or scale-up that already banks with Airwallex and lets AI agents pay for things: procurement, SaaS seats, data and APIs, travel | Agents that can pay without a shared card, and limits the agents cannot talk their way past\nUser | The CFO or financial controller | Sets each agent's limits once; approves only what is over them, on a phone, against the exact terms; reads one audit trail\nDecider | The CFO | Signs off on the policy and on the tool itself\nWhy \"already on Airwallex\" (our reasoning): Purser's card controls are Airwallex Issuing's own limits, so a company\nthat already has Airwallex accounts and cards has the least to set up. This is a narrowing choice for a first test,\nnot a finding about where demand is."},
{"id":85,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Go-to-market (hypothesis)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#go-to-market-hypothesis","text":"- A layer on top of Airwallex. Purser would be offered to Airwallex customers as an integration, for example as an\n Airwallex app or an embedded partner, if Airwallex agrees. We have no agreement with Airwallex and have not asked\n for one. Airwallex's public pricing page sends \"Platform API, Embedded Finance and High Volume use cases\" to custom\n pricing [P1], so the cost of that route to us is unknown.\n- Plus Alta (formerly Metal) for on-chain agent payments. For agents that pay per request over x402, the same CFO policy sets a\n Alta mandate per agent. Alta states that agents can pay \"from an account whose owner set spending limits on\n chain\" [P4]. Purser has run on Alta testnet only.\n- Why this channel (our reasoning): Airwallex itself says agent money movement needs \"approvals, permissions, and\n audit trails\" enforced \"through underlying infrastructure rather than prompts\" [P3]. A product that does exactly that\n on Airwallex's own rails is easiest to explain to Airwallex's customers. It also makes us dependent on Airwallex\n (see the risks below)."},
{"id":86,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Pilot pricing (hypothesis)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#pilot-pricing-hypothesis","text":"Pilot pricing: Starter €49 a month (100 invoices, then €0.25 each); Business from €249 a month; a small fee per payout.\nThese are pilot prices, set on 12 November 2026. Nothing is on sale yet and no customer has seen a\nprice. Business adds several companies, four-eyes approval and bookkeeping connectors.\n\nIt is one model, said in the same sentence in the README and in\nafter-the-kit.md.\nEvery figure comes from src/config/pricing.ts, and test/saas-additions.test.ts keeps the four places in step.\n\nWhy this shape (our reasoning): the unit a finance team counts is the supplier invoice, and Claude's cost is per\ninvoice read, so the monthly plan includes a number of invoices and charges for more\n(unit economics below). The monthly price does not grow with the money paid out; the fee\nper payout does, and it is collected with the payout itself, so there is no second bill.\n\nThe fee per payout. The fee is a percentage of each payout: the CFO signs the rate in the policy, and code keeps it at or under 1.00%, rounds it to the cent and sends it to Airwallex as a fixed amount. …"},
{"id":87,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Unit economics (hypothesis)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#unit-economics-hypothesis","text":"A hypothesis, not a result. What a company's supplier invoices would cost Purser a month, against the pilot pricing above. The measured part comes from the main run of 3 November 2026 and the end-to-end sandbox run of 10 November 2026; everything else is a price we read, with its page and date, or an assumption stated below. Hosting, the currency and the Opus line are as Max approved them on 6 November 2026; the usage in invoices and the Claude cost per invoice were restated for the pilot pricing. This section is written by src/business/unitEconomics.ts (sectionMarkdown); test/unit-economics-hypothesis.test.ts checks that this page holds exactly what it computes from the records and the assumptions, and that no number is unsourced."},
{"id":88,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Measured in the main run","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#measured-in-the-main-run","text":"Main run, 3 November 2026 [R1] | Sourcing (Haiku) | Support (Sonnet) | Treasury (Opus) | All agents\nDecisions | 11 | 4 | 9 | 24\nClaude, the agent's own calls (USD, list prices [U1]) | 0.0088 | 0.0500 | 0.2582 | 0.3170\nPer decision (USD) | 0.0008 | 0.0125 | 0.0287 | 0.0132\nEvery Claude call of the run, documents and reviews included (USD) | | | | 0.3761\nPer decision, everything included (USD) | | | | 0.0157\nClaude calls in the run | | | | 58\nPer Claude call, everything included (USD) | | | | 0.0065\nClaude per decision: USD 0.0132 for the agents' own calls, USD 0.0157 for every Claude call of the run. The agents' own calls (agent_stats) come to USD 0.3170 for 24 decisions, the figure in claims.md. The run's whole Claude bill (snapshot.claude) is USD 0.3761 for 58 calls: it also sorted and read the documents and ran the Opus reviews for the CFO, USD 0.0592 or 16% of the bill. This model uses the whole bill: USD 0.0065 a call.\n\nIn the main run, Claude made 24 decisions; of the 88 payments, 82 were routine sales and purchases that code handled inside the limits. …"},
{"id":89,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Assumptions (hypothesis)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#assumptions-hypothesis","text":"# | Assumption (hypothesis) | Value | Why\nA1 | Price | Starter €49 a month (100 invoices, then €0.25 each); Business from €249 a month; a small fee per payout. VAT excluded; the table prices one company on Starter; no revenue from Business or from the fee per payout is counted | The pilot pricing above (hypothesis); no customer has seen it. The unit a finance team counts is the supplier invoice, and Claude's cost is per invoice read, so the plan includes invoices and charges for more.\nA2 | Usage | 50 (low), 100 (mid), 500 (high) supplier invoices per company a month | Not measured: no company has used Purser for a month. Mid is exactly what Starter includes, low is half of it and high is five times it. Our own range, set with the pilot pricing; not a finding.\nA3 | Claude per invoice | the end-to-end sandbox run's Claude calls per invoice [R3] times the main run's cost per Claude call [R1], at list prices [U1] | An estimate, not a measurement: the end-to-end run counted its Claude calls (classify, read and review per invoice), not their cost, and the main run measured what a call cost on its own mix of models, in an agents' scenario. A real month may cost more or less per invoice. …"},
{"id":90,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: No margin computed (pilot)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#no-margin-computed-pilot","text":"No gross margin is computed here. No company has used Purser for a month, so there is no measured usage to set against the pilot prices, and the platform costs (A8) are not known. The measured parts above are what the runs recorded.\n\nIf every agent ran on Opus, Claude costs would be about 2.1× higher; Purser gives each agent the smallest model that passed its evals.\n\nWhere the Opus factor comes from (A4). It is the run's own Claude calls repriced at Opus list prices: USD 0.7771 instead of USD 0.3761, 2.07 times. The agents' own calls, from their recorded tokens, would cost USD 0.6970; the other calls are scaled by 2 (Sonnet) and at most 40 (Haiku); the Opus calls stay as they were. At that factor, an extra invoice would cost €0.05 in Claude against the €0.25 it earns. On the benchmark's eval cases the factor is higher [R2], because Purser's split there runs only the reviews on Opus; in the main run the Treasury agent already ran on Opus.\n\nFor a different measure, per customer query in the demo's own business, see unit-economics.md.\n\nSources for this section: …"},
{"id":91,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Market (descriptive, no size)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#market-descriptive-no-size","text":"Every company that gives an AI agent a card, a payment key or an on-chain account to spend from. We start with\nAirwallex customers that do this. We give no market size: we found no source that measures this market, and we will\nnot put a number on it without one."},
{"id":92,"doc":"docs/business/model.md","title":"Business model and pilot pricing: Risks and what we do not know","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/business/model.md#risks-and-what-we-do-not-know","text":"- Demand. We do not know whether finance teams let agents pay today, how much, or whether they would pay for\n this.\n- Airwallex could build it, and that is why we build on Airwallex. Airwallex already ships agent features of its\n own: AgentOS, where \"AgentOS components don't initiate transfers, FX conversions, or payouts on your behalf\" by\n default, Spend Management agents in cards and accounts payable, and an agentic wallet in development that would let\n people authorise an agent \"within spending limits and merchant rules set ahead of time\" [P5]. Purser does not compete\n with that: it uses Airwallex's own card controls as one of its three locks and adds what sits on top (one CFO policy\n for card and chain, approvals signed over the exact terms, a hash-chained audit log). The more agent features\n Airwallex ships, the more there is for Purser to govern, as an app or partner on the platform. The risk that remains:\n Airwallex could choose to build the approval layer itself.\n- Dependency on Airwallex and Alta. Purser's card controls are Airwallex's; its on-chain controls are Alta's.\n Purser has run only in the Airwallex sandbox and on Alta testnet. …"},
{"id":93,"doc":"docs/enterprise.md","title":"Enterprise","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/enterprise.md#enterprise","text":"What a finance team gets beyond the demo, each with where to check it; test money today.\n\nMoved from the README on 15 November, to keep it short.\n\nWhat a finance team gets beyond the demo; test money today, each with where to check it.\n\n- Purser Cloud: a console per company with Overview, Agents, Invoices & books, Transactions, Tokenisation and Settings; a public test preview where Try as guest opens a demo company read-only (purser-try.max-31b.workers.dev (https://purser-try.max-31b.workers.dev/), docs/cloud.md).\n- Approval alerts: e-mail, Slack and Teams tell the CFO a payment waits; an alert never carries anything that approves. Built and tested with stand-ins, not sent live yet: e-mail needs an e-mail provider's key, Slack and Teams the company's own incoming webhook (docs/cloud.md).\n- Zero trust and step-up: agents act only through a fixed set of tools that code checks; sensitive console settings ask for a fresh passkey check (docs/security.md, cloud/src/stepUp.ts).\n- Security contact: security.txt (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/.well-known/security.txt) and SECURITY.md; the layers a payment must pass on /security (https://kit11.max-31b.workers.dev/security). …"},
{"id":94,"doc":"docs/see-it.md","title":"See it","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/see-it.md#see-it","text":"Moved from the README on 15 November, to keep it short.\n\nThe hands-on demo, end to end: a test company files a sample invoice, Claude reads it, Pay, the approval passkey (Chromium's virtual authenticator: a test passkey, no person or phone), paid on the simulated bank, booked and filed. Test money. (MP4) Recorded from the live sites by npm run media:record (media.json); the charts are under Proof in numbers and the diagrams under How it works in 5 files.\n\nThe same payment story, animated from a live /try run of 16 Nov 2026 (test money); it opened the README's \"At a glance\" until 19 Nov 2026, when the demo's thumbnail took its place at the top.\n\n▶ MP4, 13 s▶ MP4, 14 sPurser Cloud as a guest: the demo company's dashboard (made-up data from a simulated month, test money), then its books.kit11 /books: a test company's month, read and booked by Claude live; balance sheet, charts and the invoices sorted by Claude. Test money.kit11 /proof: every claim with its run record. …"},
{"id":95,"doc":"docs/claims.md","title":"Claims and their proof","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/claims.md#claims-and-their-proof","text":"Every number and factual claim on the public pages, in the film, the video script, the README and compliance.md, with\nwhere it comes from. It opens with the main run of 3 November and the site as it stands; the sections after that keep\neach earlier check as it was."},
{"id":96,"doc":"docs/claims.md","title":"Claims and their proof: The main run (3 November) and the site as it stands","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/claims.md#the-main-run-3-november-and-the-site-as-it-stands","text":"Last checked on 26 November 2026 (the emergency-stop row, against docs/runs/2026-11-26-stop-at-rail-live.md and docs/runs/2026-11-26-card-governance-live.md; on 22 November the row on /business and /one-pager and /pricing's redirect, against test/business-page.test.ts and test/watch-out-of-menu.test.ts; on 20 November the red-team rows, against the full re-run of 20 Nov, docs/redteam/rerun-2026-11-20.json, by test/redteam-regressions.test.ts, test/readme-proof-strip.test.ts and test/evidence-wall.test.ts; the rows on roles and the approval key's life, and \"Execution re-checks the passkey signature\", against their tests; the Airwallex soaks' row, against both soak records, by their tests; every figure on /proof against the record the page names, by test/proof-trace.test.ts, listed in docs/evidence/proof-index.md; on 19 November the rows of the fourth round of fixes and the red-team re-run, against their records, by their tests; on 18 November every figure by npm run verify-all, 188 checks pass; before that the Alta rows on 15 November, against their run records, and the rest on 14 November): this table, against the README, Home, the menu, the worst case\nand llms.txt as they stand …"},
{"id":97,"doc":"docs/claims.md","title":"Claims and their proof: Earlier checks","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/claims.md#earlier-checks","text":"awx-1, the Airwallex-only run of 7 November, and the Airi run of 7 November (vic-1) were added that day (their rows\nunder \"Things that happened in separate live runs\"). The sections below were checked on 7 November 2026, against the\nmain run's record (docs/demo/main-run.json), after the jury review of that day (its rows marked \"jury review,\n7 November\"); the rows dated later were written on the day they give. Before that on 6 November, after that\nday's jury review (the four tabs' section brought to the main run's figures), and on 4 November, after a final\nindependent review. First checked on 30 October 2026 by two separate read-only audits by fresh reviewers:\n- 191 claims on the pages;\n- 200 claims in the written materials.\n\nWhat could not be proven was removed or softened (the \"Changed\" column, and the list at the end). The submission\npack's own sentences, including the deck's, are in \"The submission pack\" below.\n\nSources: …"},
{"id":98,"doc":"docs/claims.md","title":"Claims and their proof: The earlier recorded run, 30 October (archive: the CFO dashboard at /?recorded and the animation at /film; the pages play the main run since 3 November)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/claims.md#the-earlier-recorded-run-30-october-archive-the-cfo-dashboard-at-recorded-and-the-animation-at-film-the-pages-play-the-main-run-since-3-november","text":"Claim | Value | Proof | Changed\nPayments inside the limits with no person needed | 106 | snapshot counts.alone: 56 by Northwind's agents (50 purchases, 3 refunds, 1 sweep, 2 card charges) and 50 stock checks the customer's agent bought from us | The label says about half are the customer's agent.\nStops by the card, the chain, the fraud checks or the CFO | 8 | snapshot counts.blocked: 1 chain refusal, 2 card declines, 2 fake invoices, 2 planted instructions, 1 refund batch the CFO rejected | Was 9: one document flagged twice is now counted once; the label no longer says \"attempts blocked before money moved\".\nMoney kept out for good | €3,719.99 | snapshot money.blocked_eur: 2 invoices (€3,700) and the €19.99 decline at the wrong kind of shop; the €45.00 decline was paid after the raise | Was \"Stopped in time €3,764.99\".\nDecisions signed with Face ID | 4 | snapshot proof.face_id: 3 approvals and 1 rejection by passkey | The demo's audit step counts the 3 approvals; both say which.\nFake invoices and AI tricks stopped | 2 + 2 | snapshot proof.fake_invoices, proof.ai_tricks (distinct documents) | Was 2 + 3. …"},
{"id":99,"doc":"docs/claims.md","title":"Claims and their proof: Proof links (checked read-only, 30 October)","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/claims.md#proof-links-checked-read-only-30-october","text":"What | Result\nAlta transactions linked on the public pages and in the dossier | 60 of 60 exist and succeeded on chain (eth_getTransactionReceipt).\nKey transfers decoded (USDZ Transfer logs) | 3 refunds of 0.05 to Summit's account; sweep of 1.35 to the sweep wallet; first sale 0.05 to Northwind; first purchase 0.02 to Stockline; order 5 paid 0.05; quarantined 0.02 returned to its sender; clearing deposit 5.00 and claim 0.70. All match.\nAirwallex card transactions | All 4 found by card_transaction_id with the recorded amount and result: 2 approved, LIMIT_EXCEEDED, MERCHANT_CATEGORY_NOT_ALLOWED.\nAirwallex conversion, transfer, deposit | Conversion 08736b6e… 418.40 → 370.00 SETTLED. Transfer 4d508b0b… 1,850 PAID. Deposit 56366c9d… 1.35 SETTLED, with the sweep tx as reference.\nThe pages no longer say the Airwallex web app shows these ids. The ids are the ones the API returns; which one the web app\ndisplays was not checked."},
{"id":100,"doc":"docs/claims.md","title":"Claims and their proof: Controls and tests","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/claims.md#controls-and-tests","text":"Claim | Value | Proof | Changed\nRed team | 39 of 39 failed, 0 inconclusive: 37 stopped before anything moved, 2 found afterwards (a hidden card charge by the reconciliation, a rewritten log row by npm run verify); 35 scripted attacks and 4 documents written by Claude Opus as the attacker, in a throwaway test world (30 Oct). Then three runs in a row on 31 Oct: 118 of 120 failed, 2 inconclusive (bank-change notices the classifier read as data corrections: nothing was paid or changed, but not counted as stopped; runs) Re-run of 19 Nov after the fourth round of fixes, the 35 scripted attacks with no model (not held out): 34 stopped before money moved, 1 found afterwards (hidden-payment, a card charge Airwallex approves on the card's own limits). A rewritten log row is still found, not prevented, by someone holding the database file, but every payment now verifies the audit chain first, so no money moves on it, and INSERT OR REPLACE is refused. …"},
{"id":101,"doc":"docs/claims.md","title":"Claims and their proof: Things that happened in separate live runs, not in the recorded one","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/claims.md#things-that-happened-in-separate-live-runs-not-in-the-recorded-one","text":"Feature | Run | Said where\nPay-per-call clearing | Separate run, 29 October (docs/runs/2026-10-29-clearing.md) | /metal card and comparison table, film, metal-award.md\nReceive policy and quarantine | Separate world, 30 October (docs/metal-award.md section 5) | /metal card, /live scene source, compliance.md\nTask card, single use | On a backup of Friday run 2 (docs/runs/2026-10-30-single-use.md) | /live scene source, film footer\nReceivables on Global Accounts | Live in the sandbox, on a copy of the recorded ledger after the run (docs/runs/2026-10-30-receivables.md): 2 matched, 1 short by 10.00 EUR, 1 with no invoice. Kept out of the recording so its balances, reconciliation and waiting items stay one consistent moment. …"},
{"id":102,"doc":"docs/claims.md","title":"Claims and their proof: Built after the recording (30 October), and where each has run since","url":"https://github.com/agamemnon-coder/x402-business-agents/blob/main/docs/claims.md#built-after-the-recording-30-october-and-where-each-has-run-since","text":"Feature | Status | Proof | Said where\nKit 11's monthly licence fee in euros (EUR 240.00 in code, paid by the business at Airwallex by SWIFT) | Main run (3 November): planned by the Treasury agent itself (P-0005), FX EUR 110.00 for the shortfall, PAID 6 s after Max's Face ID (transfer 03360bfa…, fee EUR 13.42; PAID set through the sandbox's simulation API), see the main-run section. Earlier, agent run 1 (2 November), after Max's Face ID: P-0007, EUR 240.00 by SWIFT, Airwallex transfer 7bbb3d61-d9f3-4b8e-81cc-cc7cceb9c1df PAID, fee EUR 13.37 (ceiling EUR 20.00). Before it, the Treasury agent's own plan P-0005 was refused by Airwallex's sandbox (400 fee_unknown, nothing paid) and its re-plan P-0006 expired unsigned; at 14:25 UTC it chose not to re-plan (\"13 days remain\"). …"}];
